jason weyman acuna might be the most  recognizable member of the jackass cast  but this skateboarder's got some tricks  you haven't seen and some tacos you have  to try  jason acuna's father george served in  the united states army and was stationed  in germany when he met and married  acuna's mother the couple was  transferred to a base in pisa italy  while his mother was pregnant though  english is his first language acuna's  mother taught him german as a boy and he  remains fluent in the language he told  stevo on the stevo wild ride podcast you  know when you're a kid and you're asking  your mom what's this  my mom would tell me in german and i'd  be like no not that funny language  eventually acuna would settle in  southern california where his father's  family is from and as a pre-teen he  became heavily involved in the area's  skateboarding culture  when he was born the delivering doctor  noticed that jason acuna's head was  large compared to the rest of his body  concerned that the baby might be  hydrocephalic the doctor ran tests and  determined that acuna instead had a  genetic condition known as  achondroplasia which causes dwarfism as  a boy acuna's mother took him to an  annual conference sponsored by the  support group little people of america  thinking that he might enjoy meeting  other children with dwarfism acuna felt  differently however telling the new york  times in 2022 i came back and i go mom i  don't want to go to these things anymore  i'm like that's not what my life is  about he compared the impulse to group  people with dwarfism together to the  idea that a bald man should be friends  with other bald men he's a dude he's a  jogger he wants to hang out with other  joggers skateboarder hang out with  skateboarders  as a young skateboarder in torrance  california in the late 1980s and early  1990s jason acuna began attracting  attention in his interview with the new  york times he said he was already being  sponsored by local skate shops at age  14. at the time the local torrent  skateboard company was world industries  and acuna and his friends would try to  score free merchandise at the company  warehouse opened in 1987 by professional  skateboarders steve rocco and rodney  mullen world industries build itself as  the first skateboard company operated by  and for skaters the story goes that  steve rocco's brother sao gave a cuny  his nickname shouting hey everyone we  man is here whenever a cunha would come  around a few years later world  industries magazine big brother  published a photo spread featuring acuna  and printed the nickname after that wee  man was his official stage name  much of the groundwork for what would  one day become jackass was late at big  brother magazine the publishing arm of  world industries started by steve rocco  in 1992 the magazine embraced its parent  companies for us bios ethos and ran  skateboarding interviews and photo  spreads alongside features and humor  pieces that were unpolished irreverent  and raunchy in other words it was  jackass before jackass acuna got a job  in the office by virtue of being local  and hanging around so much that editor  and future jackass director jeff  tremaine finally just put into work when  big brother released its first video a  skateboarding compilation acuna appeared  on the box arc covered in blue paint  there's an egalitarian streak that runs  through the two plus decade run of  jackass everyone suffers on camera at  some point and everyone is the butt of  the joke over the years many of acuna's  stunts and pranks have been no different  from the ones performed by knoxville or  the rest of the cast but many of his  best and most memorable stunts came from  the unique opportunities afforded by his  height acuna was often paired with cast  member preston lacey as their two polar  opposite body types complement one  another to comedic effect  because of his stature jason acuna is  the most recognized jackass cast member  even more so than knoxville his fame is  inescapable and he estimates that he's  been recognized on the street nearly  every day since the show premiered in  the year 2000. over the years zacunia  has avoided the tabloid attention that  some of his castmates have faced in fact  he has discovered that the name we man  serves a useful role in delineating  those people who want to be his friend  from those who simply want proximity to  fame speaking to genco magazine about  romantic relationships acuna said no  chick has ever called me wee man that  i've dated i've also never dated a chick  that i noticed would call me wi-man  because it didn't feel like she was  trying to date me  so if he's not wasting it on the spoils  of fame what does jason acuna do with  his money in 2008 he became an investor  in the california-based mexican  restaurant chain chronic tacos opening a  franchise in redondo beach called  weman's chronic tacos the chain was a  good fit for him not just because of the  rock and roll street art aesthetic of  its locations but also as a connection  to his father's family which is of  mexican descent  in 2012 jason acuna took a rare leading  man role in the family christmas comedy  elf man when a little girl makes a wish  on an old elf doll to bring her father  home on christmas eve a magical elf  played by acuna appears to make the wish  come true by morning when santa will  bring him back to the north pole little  do they know that the little girl's  father has been kidnapped by a group of  thieves seeking his fantastic new  invention when the thieves attack the  house the elf must defend the family by  believing in himself and becoming the  christmas superhero elf man the film was  released direct to video and was not  terribly well received the most positive  review might be this youtube video  featuring the children of acuna's  jackass castmate dave england i thought  it was really funny that  the robbers were  not very smart  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  jackass are coming soon subscribe to our  youtube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]  you
 

